.nh
.TH "PB-ACCESS-TUNNEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-access-tunnel - Open private TCP access through stable hostd


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb access tunnel <tunnel-or-route> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Open private TCP access through stable hostd

.PP
Resolve a tunnel or route by its exact identity and forward a loopback listener to that authorized private TCP target. --listen selects the local address; the listener is closed when the command ends.

.PP
Private access requires authorization for the exact target. The listener stays on the local loopback interface, and closing this command closes the forwarding session. Public tunnel publication is managed separately with pb tunnel.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tunnel

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--listen\fP="127.0.0.1:0"
	literal-loopback listen address


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-access(1)\fP
